# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Time evolution {#time-evolution}"
msgstr "Time evolution {#time-evolution}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can realize the time-evolution operator generated by a given Hamiltonian:"
" $U=e^{-iHt}$ via the [Lie-Trotter "
"approximation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter)."
" For simplicity we use the built-in ```PauliEvolutionGate``` in the time-"
"evolution circuit. The general syntax for this is this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating matupad ang time-evolution operator na nabuo ng isang ibinigay"
" na Hamiltonian: $U=e^{-iHt}$ sa pamamagitan ng [Lie-Trotter "
"approximation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter)."
" Para sa pagiging simple, gumagamit tayo ng built-in na "
"```PauliEvolutionGate``` sa time-evolution circuit. Ang pangkalahatang "
"syntax para dito ay ganito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will use a version of this below in the Hadamard test, but stepping "
"forward for times $dt$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gagamitin natin ang isang bersyon nito sa ibaba para sa Hadamard test, "
"ngunit susulong ng $dt$ bawat hakbang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hadamard test {#hadamard-test}"
msgstr "Hadamard test {#hadamard-test}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that we wish to calculate the matrix elements of both $\\tilde{H}$ "
"and the Gram matrix $\\tilde{S}$ using the Hadamard test. Let's review how "
"this works in this context, focusing first on the construction of "
"$\\tilde{H}.$ The overall process is depicted graphically below. The layers "
"of colored state preparation blocks $\\text{Prep}|\\psi_i\\rangle$ serve as "
"a reminder that this process is carried out for all combinations of "
"$|\\psi_i\\rangle$ and $|\\psi_j\\rangle$ in our subspace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alalahanin na nais nating kalkulahin ang mga matrix element ng parehong "
"$\\tilde{H}$ at ng Gram matrix $\\tilde{S}$ gamit ang Hadamard test. Suriin "
"natin kung paano ito gumagana sa kontekstong ito, na unang tututok sa pagbuo"
" ng $\\tilde{H}.$ Ang buong proseso ay makikita sa grapikong larawan sa "
"ibaba. Ang mga layer ng may kulay na state preparation blocks na "
"$\\text{Prep}|\\psi_i\\rangle$ ay nagsisilbing paalala na ang prosesong ito "
"ay isinasagawa para sa lahat ng kombinasyon ng $|\\psi_i\\rangle$ at "
"$|\\psi_j\\rangle$ sa ating subspace.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![An image of a quantum circuit diagram with many layers indicating that the"
" circuit must be evaluated for many different states in order to perform the"
" Hadamard test.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig5.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Isang larawan ng quantum circuit diagram na may maraming layer na "
"nagpapakita na ang circuit ay kailangang suriin para sa maraming iba't ibang"
" estado upang maisagawa ang Hadamard "
"test.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig5.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The states of the system at the steps indicated are:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"    \\text{Step 0:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = |0\\rangle|0\\rangle^N \\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 1:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle \\Big)|0\\rangle^N \\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 2:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(|0\\rangle|0\\rangle^N+|1\\rangle |\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big)\\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 3:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^N+|1\\rangle P |\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big) \\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 4:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(|0\\rangle |\\psi_j\\rangle+|1\\rangle P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga estado ng sistema sa mga nakasaad na hakbang ay:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"    \\text{Step 0:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = |0\\rangle|0\\rangle^N \\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 1:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle \\Big)|0\\rangle^N \\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 2:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(|0\\rangle|0\\rangle^N+|1\\rangle |\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big)\\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 3:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(|0\\rangle |0\\rangle^N+|1\\rangle P |\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big) \\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 4:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\Big(|0\\rangle |\\psi_j\\rangle+|1\\rangle P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $P$ is a Pauli term in the decomposition of the Hamiltonian (note that "
"it cannot be a linear combination of multiple commuting Pauli terms since "
"that would not be unitary -- grouping is possible using a different "
"construction we will show later) $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_i$, $\\text{Prep} "
"\\; \\psi_j$ are controlled operations that prepare $|\\psi_i\\rangle$, "
"$|\\psi_j\\rangle$ vectors of the unitary Krylov space, with "
"$|\\psi_k\\rangle = e^{-i H k dt } \\vert \\psi \\rangle = e^{-i H k dt } "
"U_{\\psi} \\vert 0 \\rangle^N$. Applying measurements of $X$ and $Y$ to this"
" circuit calculates the real and imaginary parts, respectively, of the "
"matrix elements we require.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, ang $P$ ay isang Pauli term sa decomposition ng Hamiltonian (pansinin "
"na hindi ito maaaring maging linear combination ng maraming commuting Pauli "
"terms dahil hindi iyon magiging unitary — posible ang grouping gamit ang "
"ibang konstruksyon na ipapakita natin sa ibaba). Ang $\\text{Prep} \\; "
"\\psi_i$, $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_j$ ay mga controlled operation na nagpe-"
"prepare ng $|\\psi_i\\rangle$, $|\\psi_j\\rangle$ vectors ng unitary Krylov "
"space, kung saan ang $|\\psi_k\\rangle = e^{-i H k dt } \\vert \\psi "
"\\rangle = e^{-i H k dt } U_{\\psi} \\vert 0 \\rangle^N$. Ang pagsukat ng "
"$X$ at $Y$ sa circuit na ito ay nagbibigay ng tunay at imahinasyong bahagi, "
"ayon sa pagkakasunod, ng mga matrix element na kailangan natin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Starting from Step 4 above, apply the Hadamard gate $H$ to the zeroth "
"qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Simula sa Step 4 sa itaas, ilapat ang Hadamard gate $H$ sa zeroth qubit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"   |\\Psi\\rangle \\longrightarrow\\quad\\frac{1}{2}|0\\rangle\\Big( |\\psi_j\\rangle + P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big) + \\frac{1}{2}|1\\rangle\\Big(|\\psi_j\\rangle - P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big)\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"   |\\Psi\\rangle \\longrightarrow\\quad\\frac{1}{2}|0\\rangle\\Big( |\\psi_j\\rangle + P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big) + \\frac{1}{2}|1\\rangle\\Big(|\\psi_j\\rangle - P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big)\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Then measure either $X$ or $Y$.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos ay sukatin ang $X$ o $Y$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\begin{split}\n"
"    \\Rightarrow\\quad\\langle X\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{4}\\Bigg(\\Big\\|| \\psi_j\\rangle + P|\\psi_i\\rangle \\Big\\|^2-\\Big\\||\\psi_j\\rangle - P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big\\|^2\\Bigg) \\\\\n"
"    &= \\text{Re}\\Big[\\langle\\psi_j| P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big].\n"
"\\end{split}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\begin{split}\n"
"    \\Rightarrow\\quad\\langle X\\rangle &= \\frac{1}{4}\\Bigg(\\Big\\|| \\psi_j\\rangle + P|\\psi_i\\rangle \\Big\\|^2-\\Big\\||\\psi_j\\rangle - P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big\\|^2\\Bigg) \\\\\n"
"    &= \\text{Re}\\Big[\\langle\\psi_j| P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big].\n"
"\\end{split}\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the identity $|a + b\\|^2 = \\langle a + b | a + b \\rangle = \\|a\\|^2"
" + \\|b\\|^2 + 2\\text{Re}\\langle a | b \\rangle$. Similarly, measuring $Y$"
" yields\n"
msgstr ""
"Mula sa identity na $|a + b\\|^2 = \\langle a + b | a + b \\rangle = "
"\\|a\\|^2 + \\|b\\|^2 + 2\\text{Re}\\langle a | b \\rangle$. Sa katulad na "
"paraan, ang pagsukat ng $Y$ ay nagbibigay ng\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"    \\langle Y\\rangle = \\text{Im}\\Big[\\langle\\psi_j| P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big].\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"    \\langle Y\\rangle = \\text{Im}\\Big[\\langle\\psi_j| P|\\psi_i\\rangle\\Big].\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Adding these steps to the time-evolution we set up previously we write the "
"following.\n"
msgstr ""
"Idinaragdag ang mga hakbang na ito sa time-evolution na naset up natin "
"kanina, isusulat natin ang sumusunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"diagonalization-algorithms/krylov/extracted-"
"outputs/ac536079-96f2-435b-a15f-72c207fa24d1-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output ng nakaraang code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"diagonalization-algorithms/krylov/extracted-"
"outputs/ac536079-96f2-435b-a15f-72c207fa24d1-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We warned already about the depth involved in Trotter circuits. Performing "
"the Hadamard test in these conditions can yield an even deeper circuit, "
"especially once we decompose to native gates. This will increase even more "
"if we account for the topology of the device. So before using any time on "
"the quantum computer, it is a good idea to check the 2-qubit depth of our "
"circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nabanggit na natin ang lalim ng mga Trotter circuit. Ang pagsasagawa ng "
"Hadamard test sa mga kundisyong ito ay maaaring magbigay ng mas malalim pang"
" circuit, lalo na pagkatapos i-decompose sa mga native gate. Lalalo pa itong"
" tumindi kapag isinaalang-alang ang topology ng device. Kaya bago gumastos "
"ng oras sa quantum computer, magandang ideya munang suriin ang 2-qubit depth"
" ng ating circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A circuit of this depth cannot return usable results on modern quantum "
"computers. If we are to construct $\\tilde{H}$ and $\\tilde{S},$ we need a "
"better way. This is the reason for the efficient Hadamard test introduced "
"below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang circuit na may ganitong lalim ay hindi makakabalik ng mga magagamit na "
"resulta sa mga modernong quantum computer. Kung gusto nating itayo ang "
"$\\tilde{H}$ at $\\tilde{S},$ kailangan natin ng mas magandang paraan. Ito "
"ang dahilan ng epektibong Hadamard test na ipinakilala sa ibaba.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"4. 2 Step 2. Optimize circuits and operators for target hardware "
"{#4-2-step-2-optimize-circuits-and-operators-for-target-hardware}"
msgstr ""
"4.2 Hakbang 2. I-optimize ang mga circuit at operator para sa target na "
"hardware {#4-2-step-2-optimize-circuits-and-operators-for-target-hardware}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Efficient Hadamard test {#efficient-hadamard-test}"
msgstr "Mahusay na Hadamard test {#efficient-hadamard-test}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can optimize the deep circuits for the Hadamard test that we have "
"obtained by introducing some approximations and relying on some assumption "
"about the model Hamiltonian. For example, consider the following circuit for"
" the Hadamard test:\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating i-optimize ang malalim na circuit para sa Hadamard test na "
"nakuha natin sa pamamagitan ng pagpapakilala ng ilang approximation at pag-"
"aasa sa ilang pagpapalagay tungkol sa model Hamiltonian. Halimbawa, "
"isaalang-alang ang sumusunod na circuit para sa Hadamard test:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![An image of a quantum circuit diagram with many layers indicating that the"
" circuit must be evaluated for many different unitary operators in order to "
"perform the modified, efficient Hadamard "
"test.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig6.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Isang larawan ng quantum circuit diagram na may maraming layer na "
"nagpapakita na ang circuit ay kailangang suriin para sa maraming iba't ibang"
" unitary operator upang maisagawa ang binago at mas mahusay na Hadamard "
"test.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig6.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assume we can classically calculate $E_0$, the eigenvalue of $|0\\rangle^N$ under the Hamiltonian $H$.\n"
"This is satisfied when the Hamiltonian preserves the U(1) symmetry. Although this may seem like a strong assumption, there are many cases where it is safe to assume that there is a vacuum state (in this case it maps to the $|0\\rangle^N$ state) which is unaffected by the action of the Hamiltonian. This is true for example for chemistry Hamiltonians that describe stable molecule (where the number of electrons is conserved).\n"
"Given that the gate $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_0$, prepares the desired reference state $\\ket{\\psi_0} = \\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_0 \\ket{0} = e^{-i H 0 dt} U_{\\psi_0} \\ket{0}$, for example, to prepare the HF state for chemistry $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_0$ would be a product of single-qubit NOTs, so controlled-$\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_0$ is just a product of CNOTs.\n"
"Then the circuit above implements the following state prior to measurement:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay na maaari tayong klasikal na kalkulahin ang $E_0$, ang eigenvalue ng $|0\\rangle^N$ sa ilalim ng Hamiltonian $H$.\n"
"Natutugunan ito kapag pinapanatili ng Hamiltonian ang U(1) symmetry. Kahit mukhang malakas na pagpapalagay ito, maraming pagkakataon kung saan ligtas na ipagpalagay na may vacuum state (sa kasong ito, maimamapa ito sa estado ng $|0\\rangle^N$) na hindi naaapektuhan ng aksyon ng Hamiltonian. Totoo ito, halimbawa, para sa mga chemistry Hamiltonian na naglalarawan ng stable na molekula (kung saan ang bilang ng mga elektron ay napanatili).\n"
"Dahil ang gate na $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_0$ ay nagpe-prepare ng gustong reference state na $\\ket{\\psi_0} = \\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_0 \\ket{0} = e^{-i H 0 dt} U_{\\psi_0} \\ket{0}$, halimbawa, para sa chemistry upang ma-prepare ang HF state, ang $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_0$ ay magiging produkto ng single-qubit NOT, kaya ang controlled-$\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_0$ ay produkto lamang ng mga CNOT.\n"
"Pagkatapos ang circuit sa itaas ay nagpapatupad ng sumusunod na estado bago ang pagsukat:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"    \\text{Step 0:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\ket{0} \\ket{0}^{N}\\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 1:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(\\ket{0}\\ket{0}^N+ \\ket{1} \\ket{0}^N\\right)\\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 2:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|0\\rangle|0\\rangle^N+|1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\\right)\\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 3:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{0}\\ket{0}^N+\\ket{1} U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 4:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{0} \\ket{\\psi_0}+\\ket{1} U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\\\\\n"
"    & = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\ket{+}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}+U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)+\\ket{-}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}-U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\\right)\\\\\n"
"    & = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\ket{+i}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}-iU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)+\\ket{-i}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}+iU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\\right)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"    \\text{Step 0:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\ket{0} \\ket{0}^{N}\\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 1:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(\\ket{0}\\ket{0}^N+ \\ket{1} \\ket{0}^N\\right)\\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 2:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|0\\rangle|0\\rangle^N+|1\\rangle|\\psi_0\\rangle\\right)\\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 3:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{0}\\ket{0}^N+\\ket{1} U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\\\\\n"
"    \\text{Step 4:}\\qquad|\\Psi\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{0} \\ket{\\psi_0}+\\ket{1} U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\\\\\n"
"    & = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\ket{+}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}+U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)+\\ket{-}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}-U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\\right)\\\\\n"
"    & = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\ket{+i}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}-iU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)+\\ket{-i}\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}+iU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\\right)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where we have used the classical simulable phase shift $ U\\ket{0}^N = "
"e^{i\\phi}\\ket{0}^N$ from step 2 to 3. Therefore the expectation values "
"are\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ginamit natin ang klasikal na masisimulate na phase shift na $ "
"U\\ket{0}^N = e^{i\\phi}\\ket{0}^N$ mula sa hakbang 2 hanggang 3. Kaya naman"
" ang mga expected value ay\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"    \\langle X\\otimes P\\rangle&=\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"    \\Big(\n"
"    \\left(e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}+\\bra{\\psi_0}U^\\dagger\\right)P\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}+U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\n"
"    \\\\\n"
"    &\\qquad-\\left(e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}-\\bra{\\psi_0}U^\\dagger\\right)P\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}-U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\n"
"    \\Big)\\\\\n"
"    &=\\text{Re}\\left[e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}PU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right],\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"    \\langle X\\otimes P\\rangle&=\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"    \\Big(\n"
"    \\left(e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}+\\bra{\\psi_0}U^\\dagger\\right)P\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}+U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\n"
"    \\\\\n"
"    &\\qquad-\\left(e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}-\\bra{\\psi_0}U^\\dagger\\right)P\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}-U\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\n"
"    \\Big)\\\\\n"
"    &=\\text{Re}\\left[e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}PU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right],\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\n"
msgstr "$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"    \\langle Y\\otimes P\\rangle&=\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"    \\Big(\n"
"    \\left(e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}+i\\bra{\\psi_0}U^\\dagger\\right)P\\left(e^{i\\phi_0}\\ket{\\psi_0}-iU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\n"
"    \\\\\n"
"    &\\qquad-\\left(e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}-i\\bra{\\psi_0}U^\\dagger\\right)P\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}+iU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\n"
"    \\Big)\\\\\n"
"    &=\\text{Im}\\left[e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}PU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right].\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"    \\langle Y\\otimes P\\rangle&=\\frac{1}{4}\n"
"    \\Big(\n"
"    \\left(e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}+i\\bra{\\psi_0}U^\\dagger\\right)P\\left(e^{i\\phi_0}\\ket{\\psi_0}-iU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\n"
"    \\\\\n"
"    &\\qquad-\\left(e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}-i\\bra{\\psi_0}U^\\dagger\\right)P\\left(e^{i\\phi}\\ket{\\psi_0}+iU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right)\n"
"    \\Big)\\\\\n"
"    &=\\text{Im}\\left[e^{-i\\phi}\\bra{\\psi_0}PU\\ket{\\psi_0}\\right].\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using these assumptions we were able to write the expectation values of "
"operators of interest with fewer controlled operations. In fact, we only "
"need to implement the controlled state preparation $\\text{Prep} \\; "
"\\psi_0$ and not controlled time evolutions. Reframing our calculation as "
"above will allow us to greatly reduce the depth of the resulting circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pamamagitan ng mga pagpapalagay na ito, nagawa nating isulat ang mga "
"expected value ng mga operator na interesado tayo nang may mas kaunting "
"controlled na operasyon. Sa katunayan, kailangan lang nating ipatupad ang "
"controlled state preparation na $\\text{Prep} \\; \\psi_0$ at hindi na ang "
"controlled time evolution. Ang muling pagsasaayos ng ating kalkulasyon tulad"
" ng nabanggit sa itaas ay magbibigay-daan sa atin na lubos na bawasan ang "
"lalim ng mga nagreresultang circuit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that as a bonus, since the Pauli operator now appears as a measurement "
"at the end of the circuit rather than as a controlled gate in the middle, it"
" can be measured alongside other commuting Pauli operators as in the "
"decomposition $$H=\\sum_{\\alpha = 1}^{N_\\text{GCP}}c_\\alpha P_\\alpha $$ "
"given above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na bilang bonus, dahil ang Pauli operator ay lumalabas na ngayon "
"bilang pagsukat sa dulo ng circuit kaysa bilang controlled gate sa gitna, "
"maaari itong masukat kasabay ng iba pang commuting Pauli operator tulad ng "
"sa decomposition na $$H=\\sum_{\\alpha = 1}^{N_\\text{GCP}}c_\\alpha "
"P_\\alpha $$ na ibinigay sa itaas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Decompose time-evolution operator with Trotter decomposition {#decompose-"
"time-evolution-operator-with-trotter-decomposition}"
msgstr ""
"I-decompose ang time-evolution operator gamit ang Trotter decomposition "
"{#decompose-time-evolution-operator-with-trotter-decomposition}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instead of implementing the time-evolution operator exactly we can use the "
"Trotter decomposition to implement an approximation of it. Repeating several"
" times a certain order Trotter decomposition gives us further reduction of "
"the error introduced from the approximation. In the following, we directly "
"build the Trotter implementation in the most efficient way for the "
"interaction graph of the Hamiltonian we are considering (nearest neighbor "
"interactions only). In practice we insert Pauli rotations $R_{xx}$, "
"$R_{yy}$, $R_{zz}$ with coupling strengths $J_x,$ $J_y,$ and $J_z$ and a "
"parametrized angle $t$, which correspond to the approximate implementation "
"of $e^{-i (J_x XX + J_y YY + J_z ZZ) t}$. Given the difference in definition"
" of the Pauli rotations and the time-evolution that we are trying to "
"implement, we'll have to use the parameter $2*dt$ to achieve a time-"
"evolution of $dt$. Furthermore, we reverse the order of the operations for "
"odd number of repetitions of the Trotter steps, which is functionally "
"equivalent but allows for synthesizing adjacent operations in a single "
"$SU(2)$ unitary. This gives a much shallower circuit than what is obtained "
"using the generic `PauliEvolutionGate()` functionality.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa halip na ipatupad nang eksakto ang time-evolution operator, maaari tayong"
" gumamit ng Trotter decomposition upang maipatupad ang isang approximation "
"nito. Ang paulit-ulit na paggawa ng isang partikular na order Trotter "
"decomposition ay nagbibigay sa atin ng karagdagang pagbabawas ng error na "
"maidudulot ng approximation. Sa sumusunod, direkta nating itatayo ang "
"Trotter implementation sa pinakamabisang paraan para sa interaction graph ng"
" Hamiltonian na ating isinasaalang-alang (nearest neighbor interactions "
"lamang). Sa praktika, naglalagay tayo ng Pauli rotations na $R_{xx}$, "
"$R_{yy}$, $R_{zz}$ na may coupling strength na $J_x,$ $J_y,$ at $J_z$ at "
"isang parametrized na anggulo $t$, na tumutugma sa approximate na "
"pagpapatupad ng $e^{-i (J_x XX + J_y YY + J_z ZZ) t}$. Dahil sa pagkakaiba "
"ng depinisyon ng Pauli rotations at ng time-evolution na sinisikap nating "
"ipatupad, kailangan nating gamitin ang parameter na $2*dt$ upang makamit ang"
" time-evolution ng $dt$. Bukod dito, bine-reverse natin ang pagkakasunod ng "
"mga operasyon para sa gansal na bilang ng mga pag-uulit ng Trotter steps, na"
" katumbas sa functional na paraan ngunit nagpapahintulot ng pag-synthesize "
"ng mga katabing operasyon sa isang $SU(2)$ unitary. Nagbibigay ito ng mas "
"mababaw na circuit kaysa sa nakuha gamit ang generic na "
"`PauliEvolutionGate()` functionality.\n"

