# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To recap, we start with a reference state, then evolve it for different "
"periods of time to generate the unitary Krylov subspace. We project our "
"Hamiltonian onto that subspace. We also estimate the overlaps of the "
"subspace vectors. Finally we solve the lower-dimensional, generalized "
"eigenvalue problem classically.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ibuod, nagsisimula tayo sa isang reference state, pagkatapos ay ini-"
"evolve ito sa iba't ibang tagal ng panahon para mabuo ang unitary Krylov "
"subspace. Ini-project natin ang ating Hamiltonian sa subspace na iyon. "
"Tinatantya rin natin ang mga overlap ng mga subspace vector. Sa wakas, "
"kinakalkulahin natin ang mas maliit na dimensional na generalized eigenvalue"
" problem sa pamamagitan ng klasikal na paraan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A flow-chart overview of QKD: start with a reference state, evolve the "
"state to approximate Krylov vectors, project into the Krylov subspace, "
"diagonalize the projected subspace classically, and determine ground state "
"properties.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig7.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Isang flow-chart na pangkalahatang-tanaw ng QKD: magsimula sa isang "
"reference state, i-evolve ang estado para matantya ang Krylov vectors, mag-"
"project sa Krylov subspace, i-diagonalize ang projected subspace sa "
"pamamagitan ng klasikal na paraan, at tukuyin ang mga katangian ng ground "
"state.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig7.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let’s compare what determines computational costs of using the Krylov "
"technique classically and quantum mechanically. There are not perfect "
"analogs between classical and quantum approaches for all steps. This table "
"collects some scaling of different steps for consideration.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ikumpara natin kung ano ang nagtatakda ng computational costs kapag ginamit "
"ang Krylov technique sa klasikal at quantum na paraan. Walang perpektong "
"katumbas sa pagitan ng klasikal at quantum na mga approach para sa lahat ng "
"hakbang. Kinokolekta ng talahanayang ito ang ilang scaling ng iba't ibang "
"hakbang para sa pagsasaalang-alang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A table describing scaling of different processes classically and in the "
"quantum approach to Krylov methods. Some quantum steps have no analog. The "
"scalings are the same as those stated in "
"text.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig8.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Isang talahanayan na naglalarawan ng scaling ng iba't ibang proseso sa "
"klasikal at quantum na approach sa mga Krylov method. Ang ilang quantum na "
"hakbang ay walang katumbas. Ang mga scaling ay katulad ng nabanggit sa "
"teksto.](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-"
"algorithms/krylov/kqd-fig8.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that Hamiltonians generally have terms that cannot be simultaneously "
"measured (because they do not commute with on another). We sort terms in the"
" Hamiltonian into groups of commuting Pauli operators that can all be "
"measured simultaneously, and we may require many such groups to account for "
"all the terms that do not commute with one another. To build up $\\tilde{H}$"
" on a quantum computer requires separate measurements for each group of "
"commuting Pauli strings in the Hamiltonian, and each of those requires many "
"shots. We must do this for $r^2$ different matrix elements, corresponding to"
" $r^2$ combinations of different time evolution factors. There are sometimes"
" ways to reduce this, but in this rough treatment, the time required for "
"this scales like $N_\\text{shots}\\times N_\\text{GCP} \\times r^2.$ The "
"elements of $S$ must be estimated, which scales like "
"$O(N_\\text{shots}\\times r^2)$. Finally, solving the generalized eigenvalue"
" problem in the projected space, classically, takes $O(r^3).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Alalahanin na ang mga Hamiltonian ay karaniwang may mga termino na hindi "
"maaaring sabay na masukat (dahil hindi sila nag-commute sa isa't isa). "
"Inuuri natin ang mga termino sa Hamiltonian sa mga grupo ng mga commuting "
"Pauli operator na maaaring sabay na masukat, at maaaring kailangan natin ng "
"maraming ganitong grupo para masaklaw ang lahat ng mga termino na hindi nag-"
"commute sa isa't isa. Para mabuo ang $\\tilde{H}$ sa isang quantum computer,"
" kailangan ng hiwalay na mga sukat para sa bawat grupo ng mga commuting "
"Pauli string sa Hamiltonian, at ang bawat isa sa mga ito ay nangangailangan "
"ng maraming shots. Kailangan itong gawin para sa $r^2$ na iba't ibang matrix"
" element, na naaayon sa $r^2$ na kombinasyon ng iba't ibang time evolution "
"factor. Minsan may mga paraan para mabawasan ito, ngunit sa magaspang na "
"pagtrato na ito, ang oras na kinakailangan para dito ay nag-sscale tulad ng "
"$N_\\text{shots}\\times N_\\text{GCP} \\times r^2.$ Ang mga elemento ng $S$ "
"ay kailangang matantya, na nag-sscale tulad ng $O(N_\\text{shots}\\times "
"r^2)$. Sa wakas, ang paglutas ng generalized eigenvalue problem sa projected"
" space, sa pamamagitan ng klasikal na paraan, ay nangangailangan ng "
"$O(r^3).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that quantum Krylov diagonalization may be useful in cases where the number of commuting Pauli groups in the Hamiltonian is relatively small. These scaling dependencies suggest some applications where the Krylov method can be useful, and others where it likely will not be.\n"
"Some Hamiltonians have high complexity when mapped to qubits, involving many non-commuting Pauli strings that cannot easily be partitioned into a few commuting groups. This is often true of quantum chemistry problems, for example. This complexity presents two primary challenges for near-term quantum computers:\n"
msgstr ""
"Nakikita natin na ang quantum Krylov diagonalization ay maaaring maging kapaki-pakinabang sa mga kaso kung saan ang bilang ng mga commuting Pauli group sa Hamiltonian ay medyo maliit. Ang mga scaling dependency na ito ay nagmumungkahi ng ilang application kung saan ang Krylov method ay maaaring maging kapaki-pakinabang, at ang iba naman ay malamang na hindi.\n"
"Ang ilang Hamiltonian ay may mataas na complexity kapag na-map sa mga qubit, na kinasasangkutan ng maraming non-commuting Pauli string na hindi madaling mahati sa iilang commuting group. Ito ay madalas na totoo sa mga problema sa quantum chemistry, halimbawa. Ang complexity na ito ay nagdudulot ng dalawang pangunahing hamon para sa mga near-term quantum computer:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The estimation of each element of $\\tilde{H}$ becomes computationally "
"expensive due to the large number of terms.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagtantya ng bawat elemento ng $\\tilde{H}$ ay nagiging computationally "
"expensive dahil sa malaking bilang ng mga termino.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The required Trotter circuits become prohibitively deep.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga kinakailangang Trotter circuit ay nagiging napakalalim para maging "
"praktikal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both of the above points will be less problematic when quantum computers reach fault-tolerance, but they must be considered in the near term. Even systems with “simpler” mappings than those in quantum chemistry may experience the same impediments, if the Hamiltonians have too many non-commuting terms.\n"
"The Krylov method is most useful where the Hamiltonian can be partitioned into relatively few commuting Pauli groups, and where $H$ is easy to implement in trotter circuits. Both of these conditions are satisfied, for example, for many lattice models of interest in physics. KQD is especially useful if very little is known about the ground state. This stems from its inherent convergence guarantees and its applicability in scenarios where alternative methods are untenable due to insufficient ground state knowledge.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang parehong punto sa itaas ay magiging hindi gaanong problema kapag naabot ng mga quantum computer ang fault-tolerance, ngunit dapat itong isaalang-alang sa kasalukuyan. Kahit ang mga sistema na may \"mas simpleng\" mapping kaysa sa mga nasa quantum chemistry ay maaaring makaranas ng parehong hadlang, kung ang mga Hamiltonian ay may masyadong maraming non-commuting na termino.\n"
"Ang Krylov method ay pinaka-kapaki-pakinabang kung saan ang Hamiltonian ay maaaring hatiin sa medyo iilang commuting Pauli group, at kung saan ang $H$ ay madaling ipatupad sa mga Trotter circuit. Ang parehong kondisyon na ito ay natutugunan, halimbawa, para sa maraming lattice model na may interes sa physics. Ang KQD ay lalong kapaki-pakinabang kung napakakaunting alam tungkol sa ground state. Ito ay nagmumula sa likas na mga garantiya ng convergence nito at sa kakayahan nitong gamitin sa mga sitwasyon kung saan ang mga alternatibong paraan ay hindi angkop dahil sa kakulangan ng kaalaman tungkol sa ground state.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While KQD is a powerful tool, the protocol's time-consuming aspects, "
"particularly the estimation of each element of the projected Hamiltonian and"
" the overlap of Krylov states, represent opportunities for improvement. An "
"alternative approach involves leveraging Krylov methods in conjunction with "
"sampling-based methods, which are the subject of the next lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kahit na ang KQD ay isang makapangyarihang kasangkapan, ang mga nakakapagod "
"na aspeto ng protocol, lalo na ang pagtantya ng bawat elemento ng projected "
"Hamiltonian at ang overlap ng mga Krylov state, ay nagbibigay ng pagkakataon"
" para sa pagpapabuti. Ang isang alternatibong approach ay kinabibilangan ng "
"paggamit ng mga Krylov method kasabay ng mga sampling-based na paraan, na "
"siyang paksa ng susunod na aralin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "6. Appendices {#6-appendices}"
msgstr "6. Mga Apendiks {#6-appendices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Appendix I: Krylov subspace from real time-evolutions {#appendix-i-krylov-"
"subspace-from-real-time-evolutions}"
msgstr ""
"Apendiks I: Krylov subspace mula sa real time-evolution {#appendix-i-krylov-"
"subspace-from-real-time-evolutions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The unitary Krylov space is defined as\n"
msgstr "Ang unitary Krylov space ay tinukoy bilang\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ |\\psi\\rangle,  e^{-iH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-irH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ |\\psi\\rangle,  e^{-iH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-irH\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for some timestep $dt$ that we will determine later. Temporarily assume $r$ "
"is even: then define $d=r/2$. Notice that when we project the Hamiltonian "
"into the Krylov space above, it is indistinguishable from the Krylov space\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa ilang timestep na $dt$ na matatukoy natin sa ibaba. Pansamantalang "
"ipagpalagay na ang $r$ ay pantay: pagkatapos ay tukuyin natin ang $d=r/2$. "
"Pansinin na kapag ini-project natin ang Hamiltonian sa Krylov space sa "
"itaas, ito ay hindi matukoy mula sa Krylov space\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ e^{i\\,d\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle,  e^{i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, e^{-i\\,d\\,H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{K}_U(H, |\\psi\\rangle) = \\text{span}\\left\\{ e^{i\\,d\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle,  e^{i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, \\dots, e^{-i(d-1)H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle, e^{-i\\,d\\,H\\,dt} |\\psi\\rangle \\right\\},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that is, where all the time-evolutions are shifted backward by $d$ timesteps.\n"
"The reason it is indistinguishable is because the matrix elements\n"
msgstr ""
"iyon ay, kung saan ang lahat ng time-evolution ay inilipat ng $d$ na timestep pabalik.\n"
"Ang dahilan kung bakit hindi ito matukoy ay dahil ang mga matrix element\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{H}_{j,k} = \\langle\\psi|e^{i\\,j\\,H\\,dt}He^{-i\\,k\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle=\\langle\\psi|He^{i(j-k)H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{H}_{j,k} = \\langle\\psi|e^{i\\,j\\,H\\,dt}He^{-i\\,k\\,H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle=\\langle\\psi|He^{i(j-k)H\\,dt}|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"are invariant under overall shifts of the evolution time, since the time-"
"evolutions commute with the Hamiltonian. For odd $r$, we can use the "
"analysis for $r-1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"ay hindi nagbabago sa ilalim ng pangkalahatang paglilipat ng evolution time,"
" dahil ang mga time-evolution ay nag-commute sa Hamiltonian. Para sa "
"kaganapan na $r$ ay gansal, maaari nating gamitin ang pagsusuri para sa "
"$r-1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We want to show that somewhere in this Krylov space, there is guaranteed to "
"be a low-energy state. We do so by way of the following result, which is "
"derived from Theorem 3.1 in [\\[3\\]](#references):\n"
msgstr ""
"Nais nating ipakita na sa loob ng Krylov space na ito, may garantiya na "
"mayroon isang low-energy state. Ginagawa natin ito sa pamamagitan ng "
"sumusunod na resulta, na hango mula sa Theorem 3.1 sa "
"[\\[3\\]](#references):\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Claim 1:** there exists a function $f$ such that for energies $E$ in the "
"spectral range of the Hamiltonian (that is, between the ground state energy "
"and the maximum energy)...\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pahayag 1:** mayroong isang function na $f$ na para sa mga enerhiya $E$ sa"
" spectral range ng Hamiltonian (iyon ay, sa pagitan ng ground state energy "
"at ng maximum energy)...\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$f(E_0)=1$\n"
msgstr "$f(E_0)=1$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$|f(E)|\\le2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d}$ for all values of $E$ that lie "
"$\\ge\\delta$ away from $E_0$, that is, it is exponentially suppressed\n"
msgstr ""
"$|f(E)|\\le2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d}$ para sa lahat ng halaga ng $E$ "
"na nasa $\\ge\\delta$ na layo mula sa $E_0$, iyon ay, ito ay exponentially "
"suppressed\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$f(E)$ is a linear combination of $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ for $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$\n"
msgstr ""
"$f(E)$ ay isang linear combination ng $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ para sa "
"$j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We give a proof below, but that can be safely skipped unless one wants to "
"understand the full, rigorous argument. For now we focus on the implications"
" of the above claim. By property 3 above, we can see that the shifted Krylov"
" space above contains the state $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$. This is our low-energy"
" state. To see why, write $|\\psi\\rangle$ in the energy eigenbasis:\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbibigay tayo ng patunay sa ibaba, ngunit maaari itong laktawan maliban "
"kung nais ng isa na maunawaan ang buong, mahigpit na argumento. Sa ngayon ay"
" nakatuon tayo sa mga implikasyon ng pahayag sa itaas. Sa pamamagitan ng "
"katangian 3 sa itaas, makikita natin na ang shifted Krylov space sa itaas ay"
" naglalaman ng estado na $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$. Ito ang ating low-energy "
"state. Para maunawaan kung bakit, isulat ang $|\\psi\\rangle$ sa energy "
"eigenbasis:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_k|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_k|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $|E_k\\rangle$ is the kth energy eigenstate and $\\gamma_k$ is its "
"amplitude in the initial state $|\\psi\\rangle$. Expressed in terms of this,"
" $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$ is given by\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $|E_k\\rangle$ ay ang kth energy eigenstate at ang $\\gamma_k$"
" ay ang amplitude nito sa initial state na $|\\psi\\rangle$. Ipinahayag sa "
"mga terminong ito, ang $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$ ay ibinibigay ng\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f(H)|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_kf(E_k)|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f(H)|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{k=0}^{N}\\gamma_kf(E_k)|E_k\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"using the fact that we can replace $H$ by $E_k$ when it acts on the "
"eigenstate $|E_k\\rangle$. The energy error of this state is therefore\n"
msgstr ""
"gamit ang katotohanan na maaari nating palitan ang $H$ ng $E_k$ kapag "
"kumikilos ito sa eigenstate na $|E_k\\rangle$. Ang energy error ng estado na"
" ito ay samakatuwid\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} = \\frac{\\langle\\psi|f(H)(H-E_0)f(H)|\\psi\\rangle}{\\langle\\psi|f(H)^2|\\psi\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} = \\frac{\\langle\\psi|f(H)(H-E_0)f(H)|\\psi\\rangle}{\\langle\\psi|f(H)^2|\\psi\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"= \\frac{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"= \\frac{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To turn this into an upper bound that is easier to understand, we first "
"separate the sum in the numerator into terms with $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ and "
"terms with $E_k-E_0>\\delta$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para gawing upper bound na mas madaling maunawaan, unang hinahati natin ang "
"sum sa numerator sa mga termino na may $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ at mga termino "
"na may $E_k-E_0>\\delta$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} = \\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} + \\frac{\\sum_{E_k> E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} = \\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} + \\frac{\\sum_{E_k> E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can upper bound the first term by $\\delta$,\n"
msgstr "Maaari nating i-upper bound ang unang termino ng $\\delta$,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} < \\frac{\\delta\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} \\le \\delta,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0)}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} < \\frac{\\delta\\sum_{E_k\\le E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2}{\\sum_{k=0}^{N}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2} \\le \\delta,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the first step follows because $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ for every $E_k$ in"
" the sum, and the second step follows because the sum in the numerator is a "
"subset of the sum in the denominator. For the second term, first we lower "
"bound the denominator by $|\\gamma_0|^2$, since $f(E_0)^2=1$: adding "
"everything back together, this gives\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang unang hakbang ay sumusunod dahil ang $E_k-E_0\\le\\delta$ para"
" sa bawat $E_k$ sa sum, at ang ikalawang hakbang ay sumusunod dahil ang sum "
"sa numerator ay isang subset ng sum sa denominator. Para sa ikalawang "
"termino, una ay ina-lower bound natin ang denominator ng $|\\gamma_0|^2$, "
"dahil $f(E_0)^2=1$: pagtitipon-tipunin ang lahat ng ito, nagbibigay ito ng\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} \\le \\delta + \\frac{1}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} \\le \\delta + \\frac{1}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2f(E_k)^2(E_k-E_0).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simplify what is left, notice that for all these $E_k$, by the definition"
" of $f$ we know that $f(E_k)^2 \\le 4\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-2d}$. "
"Additionally upper bounding $E_k-E_0<2\\|H\\|$ and upper bounding "
"$\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2<1$ gives\n"
msgstr ""
"Para pasimplehin ang natitira, pansinin na para sa lahat ng $E_k$ na ito, "
"ayon sa kahulugan ng $f$ alam natin na $f(E_k)^2 \\le 4\\left(1 + "
"\\delta\\right)^{-2d}$. Dagdag pa rito, ang pag-upper bound ng $E_k-"
"E_0<2\\|H\\|$ at ang pag-upper bound ng "
"$\\sum_{E_k>E_0+\\delta}|\\gamma_k|^2<1$ ay nagbibigay ng\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} \\le \\delta + \\frac{8}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\|H\\|\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-2d}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\text{energy error} \\le \\delta + \\frac{8}{|\\gamma_0|^2}\\|H\\|\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-2d}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This holds for any $\\delta>0$, so if we set $\\delta$ equal to our goal "
"error, then the error bound above converges towards that exponentially with "
"the Krylov dimension $2d=r$. Also note that if $\\delta<E_1-E_0$ then the "
"$\\delta$ term actually goes away entirely in the above bound.\n"
msgstr ""
"Naaangkop ito para sa anumang $\\delta>0$, kaya kung itutumbas natin ang "
"$\\delta$ sa ating layunin na error, ang error bound sa itaas ay "
"exponentially nagco-converge patungo roon kasabay ng Krylov dimension na "
"$2d=r$. Pansinin din na kung $\\delta<E_1-E_0$ ang $\\delta$ na termino ay "
"ganap na nawawala sa bound sa itaas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To complete the argument, we first note that the above is just the energy "
"error of the particular state $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$, rather than the energy "
"error of the lowest energy state in the Krylov space. However, by the "
"(Rayleigh-Ritz) variational principle, the energy error of the lowest energy"
" state in the Krylov space is upper bounded by the energy error of any state"
" in the Krylov space, so the above is also an upper bound on the energy "
"error of the lowest energy state, that is, the output of the Krylov quantum "
"diagonalization algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para kumpletuhin ang argumento, una ay pinapanatili natin na ang nasa itaas "
"ay ang energy error lamang ng partikular na estado na $f(H)|\\psi\\rangle$, "
"at hindi ang energy error ng pinakamababang energy state sa Krylov space. "
"Gayunpaman, ayon sa (Rayleigh-Ritz) variational principle, ang energy error "
"ng pinakamababang energy state sa Krylov space ay na-upper bound ng energy "
"error ng anumang estado sa Krylov space, kaya ang nasa itaas ay upper bound "
"din sa energy error ng pinakamababang energy state, iyon ay, ang output ng "
"Krylov quantum diagonalization algorithm.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A similar analysis as the above can be carried out that additionally "
"accounts for noise and the thresholding procedure discussed in the notebook."
" See [\\[2\\]](#references) and [\\[4\\]](#references) for this analysis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang katulad na pagsusuri tulad ng nasa itaas ay maaaring isagawa na kasama "
"rin ang noise at ang thresholding procedure na tinalakay sa notebook. "
"Tingnan ang [\\[2\\]](#references) at [\\[4\\]](#references) para sa "
"pagsusuring ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix II: proof of Claim 1 {#appendix-ii-proof-of-claim-1}"
msgstr "Apendiks II: patunay ng Pahayag 1 {#appendix-ii-proof-of-claim-1}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following is mostly derived from [\\[3\\]](#references), Theorem 3.1: "
"let $0 < a < b$ and let $\\Pi^*_d$ be the space of residual polynomials "
"(polynomials whose value at 0 is 1) of degree at most $d$. The solution to\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod ay karamihang hango mula sa [\\[3\\]](#references), Theorem "
"3.1: hayaan ang $0 < a < b$ at hayaan ang $\\Pi^*_d$ na maging espasyo ng "
"mga residual polynomial (mga polynomial na ang halaga sa 0 ay 1) ng degree "
"na hindi hihigit sa $d$. Ang solusyon sa\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = \\min_{p \\in \\Pi^*_d} \\max_{x \\in [a, b]} |p(x)| \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = \\min_{p \\in \\Pi^*_d} \\max_{x \\in [a, b]} |p(x)| \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is\n"
msgstr "ay\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p^*(x) = \\frac{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a - 2x}{b - a}\\right)}{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right)}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p^*(x) = \\frac{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a - 2x}{b - a}\\right)}{T_d\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right)}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and the corresponding minimal value is\n"
msgstr "at ang kaukulang minimal na halaga ay\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(\\frac{b + a}{b - a}\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We want to convert this into a function that can be expressed naturally in terms of complex exponentials, because those are the real time-evolutions that generate the quantum Krylov space.\n"
"To do so, it is convenient to introduce the following transformation of energies within the spectral range of the Hamiltonian to numbers in the range $[0,1]$: define\n"
msgstr ""
"Nais nating i-convert ito sa isang function na maaaring natural na ipahayag sa mga tuntunin ng complex exponential, dahil ang mga ito ang mga real time-evolution na bumubuo ng quantum Krylov space.\n"
"Para magawa ito, maginhawa na ipakilala ang sumusunod na transformation ng mga enerhiya sa loob ng spectral range ng Hamiltonian patungo sa mga numero sa hanay na $[0,1]$: tukuyin ang\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"g(E) = \\frac{1-\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big)}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"g(E) = \\frac{1-\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big)}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $dt$ is a timestep such that $-\\pi < E_0dt < E_\\text{max}dt < \\pi$.\n"
"Notice that $g(E_0)=0$ and $g(E)$ grows as $E$ moves away from $E_0$.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $dt$ ay isang timestep na nagbibigay ng $-\\pi < E_0dt < E_\\text{max}dt < \\pi$.\n"
"Pansinin na $g(E_0)=0$ at ang $g(E)$ ay lumalaki habang lumalayo ang $E$ mula sa $E_0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now using the polynomial $p^*(x)$ with the parameters a, b, d set to $a = "
"g(E_0 + \\delta)$, $b = 1$, and d = int(r/2), we define the function:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon gamit ang polynomial na $p^*(x)$ na may mga parameter na a, b, d na "
"itinakda sa $a = g(E_0 + \\delta)$, $b = 1$, at d = int(r/2), tinutukoy "
"natin ang function:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f(E) = p^* \\left( g(E) \\right) = \\frac{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big) - \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 +\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f(E) = p^* \\left( g(E) \\right) = \\frac{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{\\cos\\big((E-E_0)dt\\big) - \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 +\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}{T_d\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $E_0$ is the ground state energy. We can see by inserting "
"$\\cos(x)=\\frac{e^{ix}+e^{-ix}}{2}$ that $f(E)$ is a trigonometric "
"polynomial of degree $d$, that is, a linear combination of $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ "
"for $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$. Furthermore, from the definition of $p^*(x)$ "
"above we have that $f(E_0)=p(0)=1$ and for any $E$ in the spectral range "
"such that $\\vert E-E_0 \\vert > \\delta$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $E_0$ ay ang ground state energy. Makikita natin sa "
"pamamagitan ng pagpasok ng $\\cos(x)=\\frac{e^{ix}+e^{-ix}}{2}$ na ang "
"$f(E)$ ay isang trigonometric polynomial ng degree na $d$, iyon ay, isang "
"linear combination ng $e^{ijE\\,dt}$ para sa $j=-d,-d+1,...,d-1,d$. Bukod pa"
" rito, mula sa kahulugan ng $p^*(x)$ sa itaas mayroon tayong $f(E_0)=p(0)=1$"
" at para sa anumang $E$ sa spectral range na nagbibigay ng $\\vert E-E_0 "
"\\vert > \\delta$ mayroon tayong\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|f(E)| \\le \\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|f(E)| \\le \\beta(a, b, d) = T_d^{-1}\\left(1 + 2\\frac{1-\\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}{1 + \\cos\\big(\\delta\\,dt\\big)}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\leq 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d} = 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-\\lfloor k/2\\rfloor}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\leq 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-d} = 2\\left(1 + \\delta\\right)^{-\\lfloor k/2\\rfloor}.\n"
"$$\n"

